\section{Files}{

The value of a file target (\code{format = "file"}) is its paths. The board
shows each file in its own section, 50 at a time, and builds a file's view
only when its section opens: \code{tar_board_preview()} is called with the
path, of class \verb{tar_board_file_<extension>} (lower case) and
\code{tar_board_file}. The board's method shows images, PDF and HTML files,
CSV and TSV files as tables, Markdown, and the first lines of text files,
with R code in colour. A method for, say, \code{tar_board_file_parquet} adds a
type.
}

\section{Where methods come from}{

A package registers its methods as usual, with \code{S3method()} in its
NAMESPACE (roxygen2's \verb{@exportS3Method targetsboard::tar_board_preview}).
For a project's own classes, put the methods in a file \verb{_targetsboard.R}
in the board's folder, beside \verb{_targets.R}. The board sources that file,
and only that file, when it starts and on Refresh, and registers the
\verb{tar_board_preview.<class>()} functions it defines. A method there
replaces the board's own, or a package's, for the same class, and is
dropped when it is removed from the file. The pipeline itself never runs
inside the board.
